@sprint1 @issue-9 @auth
Feature: [Issue #9] Fitur Register & Login Sesuai Peran (Warga & Ketua RT)
  As a resident or RT administrator
  I want to register and authenticate securely into RTConnect
  So that I can access administrative services according to my verified role

  Background:
    Given the RTConnect backend application is ready

  Scenario: Registrasi akun warga baru dengan identitas lengkap dan valid
    Given I prepare a unique citizen registration payload:
      | field          | value                          |
      | nama_lengkap   | Ahmad Fauzi                    |
      | email_prefix   | fauzi                          |
      | password       | PasswordKuat#2026              |
      | nomor_telepon  | 081234567890                   |
      | alamat         | Jl. Melati No. 12 RT 05 RW 02  |
    When I send a POST request to "/api/v1/auth/register" with the payload
    Then the response status code should be 201
    And the response JSON should indicate success
    And the response field "data.role" should be "warga"
    And the registered user should exist in the database with role "warga"

  Scenario Outline: Registrasi warga gagal karena format data tidak memenuhi validasi
    Given I prepare a citizen registration payload with NIK "<nik>", email "<email>", and password "<password>"
    When I send a POST request to "/api/v1/auth/register" with the payload
    Then the response status code should be 400
    And the response JSON should indicate failure
    And the response field "error" should be "<error_code>"

    Examples:
      | nik              | email                   | password          | error_code       |
      | 12345            | valid_test@example.com  | PasswordKuat#2026 | INVALID_NIK      |
      | 3515082104990099 | invalid-email-format    | PasswordKuat#2026 | INVALID_PROFILE  |
      | 3515082104990099 | valid_test@example.com  | short             | INVALID_PASSWORD |

  Scenario: Registrasi warga gagal akibat duplikasi NIK atau email yang sudah terdaftar
    Given an existing resident user with email "resident@example.test" is registered
    When I submit a registration with an already registered email "resident@example.test"
    Then the response status code should be 400
    And the response JSON should indicate failure
    And the response field "error" should be "DUPLICATE_ENTRY"

  Scenario: Login berhasil sebagai Warga dengan kredensial valid
    When I authenticate with identity "resident@example.test" and password "LocalTestOnly#2026"
    Then the response status code should be 200
    And the response JSON should indicate success
    And the response should contain a valid JWT token
    And the response field "data.user.role" should be "warga"

  Scenario: Login berhasil sebagai Ketua RT dengan kredensial valid
    When I authenticate with identity "rt@example.test" and password "LocalTestOnly#2026"
    Then the response status code should be 200
    And the response JSON should indicate success
    And the response should contain a valid JWT token
    And the response field "data.user.role" should be "rt"

  Scenario: Login gagal jika password salah
    When I authenticate with identity "resident@example.test" and password "WrongPassword#999"
    Then the response status code should be 401
    And the response JSON should indicate failure
    And the response field "error" should be "UNAUTHORIZED"

  Scenario: Mengakses endpoint profil diri /api/v1/auth/me dengan token valid
    Given I am authenticated as "resident@example.test" with password "LocalTestOnly#2026"
    When I send an authenticated GET request to "/api/v1/auth/me"
    Then the response status code should be 200
    And the response JSON should indicate success
    And the response field "data.email" should be "resident@example.test"

  Scenario: Akses endpoint terproteksi ditolak tanpa token autentikasi
    When I send an unauthenticated GET request to "/api/v1/auth/me"
    Then the response status code should be 401
    And the response JSON should indicate failure
    And the response field "error" should be "UNAUTHORIZED"
